# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL.
#
# The default path needs no configuration at all: run `az login` and the server
# borrows the Azure CLI's token, resolving your tenant and default environment
# from whatever the CLI is signed in to. You do not need a .env file for that.
#
# Nothing below is a secret either - client and tenant IDs are public identifiers.
# The only credential at rest is the refresh token, held by the Azure CLI in az
# mode, or in .token_cache.json in device-code mode. Both are gitignored.

# --- Auth mode -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave PA_CLIENT_ID unset for az mode (the default).
# SET it to switch to device-code auth with your own app registration, for tenants
# where the Azure CLI is not consented for the Flow audience.
# PA_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# Only consulted when the Azure CLI is not the token source, or to pin the tenant.
# PA_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# --- Target environment --------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults to Default-<tenant>. Override to target a sandbox environment.
# Find the GUID in the make.powerautomate.com URL after switching environment.
#
# Use a DEMO tenant. This server creates, edits and runs real flows.
# PA_ENV_ID=Default-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
